course: dictionary
lesson: 15126
title: Sanitary: clean and healthy
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Sanitary is a formal word that means clean and free from germs and dirt that cause disease. «The kitchen must be kept sanitary so the food stays safe.» Here the kitchen must have no germs that could make people ill.
explain: Sanitary can also describe how a town keeps people healthy by getting rid of waste and dirty water. «Good sanitary systems took dirty water away from the streets.» Here the word is about the pipes and drains, not about how something looks.
explain: Read the words around sanitary to find its meaning. «Washing your hands before you eat keeps things sanitary.» Hands wash away germs, so sanitary must mean free from germs. Try the swap: "Washing your hands keeps things clean and free from germs." It still makes sense.
explain: Children often say clean, and that is a good everyday word. Sanitary is more formal, so you will see it in health and safety lessons, hospitals and history books. When you write about hygiene, you can use sanitary to sound precise.
fact: Sanitary means clean and free from germs and dirt that cause disease.
fact: Another meaning is about systems that remove waste and dirty water to keep people healthy.
fact: «Sanitary products» and «sanitary bins» are used in toilets, and «sanitary conditions» describes how clean a place is.
fact: In history, poor sanitary conditions in old cities helped diseases such as cholera to spread.
fact: «Not very sanitary» means dirty, with germs that could make people ill.
exercise: «The kitchen must be kept sanitary so the food stays safe.» What does sanitary mean here? | Full of music and noise | *Free from germs and dirt | Old and broken | Very cold and wet
exercise: Ayesha says sanitary means the same as clean in a kitchen. Which everyday word is the closest swap? | Lost | Noisy | Sticky | *Clean
exercise: «Dirty water and bad sanitary conditions made people ill in old cities.» Which problem does sanitary point to? | Trees growing too tall | *Waste and dirty water not being dealt with | Music played too loudly | Lots of people dancing in the street
test:
«Washing your hands before you eat keeps things sanitary.» What does sanitary mean here? | Dirty and full of germs | *Clean and free from germs | Very wet and muddy | Full of sand
test:
What is a sanitary bin for? | Keeping water warm | *Holding waste, such as used tissues | Storing old books | Growing plants
exam:
«The kitchen was not very sanitary, so the cook washed the worktops.» What does not very sanitary suggest? | Clean and healthy | Very old and very tall | *Dirty, with germs that could make people ill | Full of happy people
